      {
        "type": "note",
        "kind": "spain",
        "text": "For plans you've already made, Spain mostly says voy a + verb: voy a cenar con Ana. The futuro sounds more certain or a bit more formal. You'll hear it in promises, the weather forecast and the news."
      },
      {
        "type": "twist",
        "title": "Voy a or llamaré",
        "a": [
          "Voy a llamar a Ana.",
          "I'm going to call Ana."
        ],
        "b": [
          "Te llamaré, te lo prometo.",
          "I'll call you, I promise."
        ],
        "note": "Voy a: a plan. Llamaré: a promise, or something you expect to happen."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "Keep the accent: hablaré, hablará. Every form has one except nosotros: hablaremos."
      }
